  "claim_short": "Question 1 has an affirmative answer. Let V be a Hausdorff locally convex Namioka--Phelps space, let V* carry its weak-star topology and its standard uniformity xi* of uniform convergence on bounded subsets of V, and let Q be an equicontinuous weak-star compact convex subset of V*. Every weak-star continuous semigroup action on Q which is xi*-nonexpansive and xi*-distal has a common fixed point.",
